// Internal PROJECT-ROOT MARKER for dobby's shipped biome presets — not a preset,
// not a consumer extends target (package.json `exports` expose ONLY ./biome/core
// and ./biome/react). It is named `biome.jsonc` precisely so BIOME finds it.
//
// Why it exists: when the config-less default points `--config-path` at a preset in
// THIS directory, biome resolves the project root by walking UP from that file until
// it finds a `biome.json(c)`, then SCANS that whole project for nested root
// configurations. Without this marker the adopted project is whatever tree dobby's
// package happens to sit in (in the dev repo: dobby itself), so an unrelated nested
// root `biome.jsonc` anywhere in it — e.g. a git worktree under `.claude/worktrees/`,
// which the kit itself creates — makes biome exit with "Found a nested root
// configuration" and NO JSON, hard-failing EVERY config-less `dobby check` in a
// project that has nothing to do with it. Neither `files.includes` negations nor the
// consumer's `--vcs-root` ignore file suppress that scan (the ignore file belongs to
// the consumer's repo, not to the adopted foreign project) — both lab-verified
// against bundled biome 2.5.4.
//
// Stopping the walk here keeps the config-less default HERMETIC: the adopted project
// is this directory (preset files only), never dobby's or the consumer's
// surroundings. The checked paths still come from the spawn cwd, so findings are
// unchanged.
{
  "root": true
}
